</th>
<td align="center"> <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20%282da%20type%29" title="String (2da type)"> string</a>
</td>
<td>  This should be generic animation name regardless of creature model. The exact animation based on creature is references inside the animation blend trees
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th>  Strref
</th>
<td align="center"> <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20%282da%20type%29" title="Int (2da type)"> int</a>
</td>
<td>  String Reference for the name of the animation. Used primarily for the toolset and animation states on placeables.
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th>  Type
</th>
<td align="center"> <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20%282da%20type%29" title="Int (2da type)">int</a>
</td>
<td>  The type of the animation. This is a bitfield indicating if the animation is a looping animation, fire and forget, overlay, movement animation, stationary… etc.
<ul><li> 0x0001 - Looping</li>
<li> 0x0002 - Overlay</li>
<li> 0x0004 - Ambient</li>
<li> 0x0008 - Moving</li>
<li> 0x0010 - Equip</li>
<li> 0x0020 - Unequip</li>
<li> 0x0040 - PartyAttack</li>
<li> 0x0080 - SimpleAttack</li>
<li> 0x0100 - Parry</li>
<li> 0x0200 - Dodge</li>
<li> 0x0400 - Damage</li>
<li> 0x0800 - Deathblow</li>
<li> 0x1000 - Spellcasting</li>
<li> 0x2000 - Visual Effect</li>
<li> 0x4000 - Twitchs</li></ul>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th>  AnimName
